<title>SINGAPORE: Teledata buys out shares in subsidiaries.</title>
<headline>Teledata buys out shares in subsidiaries.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teledata (Singapore) Ltd said on Wednesday it has acquired all the shares it did not own in two subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Teledata said in a statement it bought 290,000 shares in Telebit (Singapore) Pte Ltd at Singapore $1.00 each and now owned 100 percent of the firm's issued and paid-up capital.</p>
<p>It said the company also acquired 275,000 shares in Plexus Technology Pte Ltd at S$1.00 each and now held all the issued and paid-up capital in Plexus.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
